hadiths[112]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19365","Affan narrated to us from Abu Awanah: Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated to us, he said: I heard Jarir ibn Abdillah stand to deliver a sermon on the day al-Mughirah ibn Shubah died, so he said: Upon you is fear of Allah, mighty and majestic is He, and dignity and calm, until a commander comes to you, for one will come to you now. Then he said: Intercede for your commander, for he used to love pardoning. And he said: To proceed, I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I pledge to you upon Islam. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And I stipulate counsel to every Muslim. So I pledged to him upon this, and by the Lord of this mosque, I am indeed sincere to you all. Then he sought forgiveness and came down."
"19366","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us from Abu Wail from Jarir ibn Abdillah al-Bajali, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, stipulate upon me. So he said: You worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, and you perform the prescribed prayer, and you pay the obligatory alms, and you give counsel to the Muslim, and you disavow the disbeliever."
"19367","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Jabir, he said: A man narrated to me from Tariq al-Tamimi from Jarir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by women and greeted them."
"19368","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Habib from al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl, or Shibl, Abu Nuaym said: al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl, meaning Ibn Awf, in this hadith, from Jarir ibn Abdillah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Any slave who flees, the covenant of protection is quit of him."
"19369","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir from his father from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever institutes in Islam a good practice, he shall have its reward and the reward of whoever acts upon it after him, without anything being diminished from their rewards; and whoever institutes in Islam an evil practice, upon him shall be its burden and the burden of whoever acts upon it after him, without anything being diminished from their burdens."
"19370","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Awn ibn Abi Jahfah from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir al-Bajali from his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the early part of the day, and he mentioned it, except that he said: So he commanded Bilal, and he called the adhan, then he entered, then he came out to pray, and he said: As if it were gilded."
"19371","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from Amr ibn Murrah from Zadham from Jarir ibn Abdillah al-Bajali that a man came and entered Islam, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was teaching him Islam while on his journey, then the hoof of his camel entered the hole of a jerboa, so his camel threw him and he died. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon him and said: He did little and was rewarded much; Hammad said it three times: The lahd is for us, and the shaqq is for others."
"19372","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us: Uthman al-Bajali narrated to us from Zadham, and he mentioned the hadith."
"19373","Ismail narrated to us from Yunus from Amr ibn Said from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, he said: Jarir said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the sudden glance, so he commanded me to turn away my gaze."
"19374","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from Ubaydullah ibn Jarir from Jarir, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I pledge to you upon Islam, so he withheld his hand and said: Counsel to every Muslim."
"19375","Then the Messenger of Allah said: Indeed, whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah, mighty and majestic is He, will not show mercy to him."
"19376","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Mansur, he said: I heard Abu Wail narrating from a man from Jarir that he said: I pledged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon establishing the prayer and paying the alms and counsel to the Muslim and upon parting from the polytheist."
"19377","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman from Abu Wail from Jarir, he said: I pledged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon establishing the prayer and paying the alms and counsel to every Muslim and upon parting from the polytheist, or a word to that meaning."
"19378","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman, he said: I heard Abu Dhabyan narrating from Jarir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah, mighty and majestic is He, will not show mercy to him."
"19379","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us from Abu Wail that Jarir said: O Messenger of Allah, stipulate upon me. He said: You worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, and you perform the prescribed prayer, and you pay the obligatory alms, and you give counsel to the Muslim, and you disavow the disbeliever."
"19380","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Ubaydullah ibn Jarir from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, does not show mercy to whoever does not show mercy to people."
"19381","Hajjaj narrated to us: Shubah narrated to me from Ali ibn Mudrik, he said: I heard Abu Zurah narrating from Jarir, and he is his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: In the Farewell Pilgrimage: O Jarir, make the people silent. Then he said in his sermon: Do not return after me disbelievers, some of you striking the necks of others."
"19382","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Ibrahim from Hammam, he said: Jarir ibn Abdillah urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, so it was said to him: Do you do this when you have urinated? He said: Yes, I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, urinate, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks. Ibrahim said: And this hadith used to please them, because the Islam of Jarir was after the revelation of al-Maidah."
"19383","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: I heard Jarir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah, mighty and majestic is He, will not show mercy to him."
"19384","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Zayd ibn Wahb from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and he mentioned the like of it."
"19385","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Zayd ibn Wahb from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah, mighty and majestic is He, will not show mercy to him."
"19386","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Dhabyan from Jarir, the like of that."
"19387","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Ismail narrated to us from Qays from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never veiled himself from me since I became Muslim, nor saw me but that he smiled."
"19388","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir from his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the early part of the day. He said: Then there came to him people barefoot, naked, wearing striped woolen garments with openings cut in them, or cloaks, wearing swords, most of them from Mudar, indeed all of them from Mudar. So the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed at the poverty he saw in them. He said: So he entered, then came out, and commanded Bilal, and he called the adhan and the iqamah, and he prayed, then he addressed and said: O people, fear your Lord who created you from a single soul, to the end of the verse: Allah is ever watchful over you; and he recited the verse that is in al-Hashr: And let a soul look to what it has put forth for tomorrow. Let a man give charity from his dinars, from his dirhams, from his garment, from his sa of wheat, from his sa of dates, until he said: Even with half a date. He said: Then a man from the Ansar came with a bundle that his hand could hardly lift, indeed it had failed; then the people followed one another until I saw two heaps of food and clothing, until I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, radiant, meaning as if it were gilded. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever institutes in Islam a good practice, he shall have its reward and the reward of whoever acts upon it after him, without anything being diminished from their rewards; and whoever institutes in Islam an evil practice, upon him shall be its burden and the burden of whoever acts upon it after him, without anything being diminished from their burdens."
"19389","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Awn ibn Abi Jahfah, he said: I heard Mundhir ibn Jarir narrating from his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the early part of the day, and he mentioned it, except that he said: And he commanded Bilal, and he called the adhan, then he entered, then he came out and prayed, and he said: As if it were gilded."
"19390","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Abu Janab narrated to us from Zadham from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when we emerged from Madinah, there was a rider hastening toward us, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As if this rider intends you. He said: Then the man reached us and greeted, and we returned it upon him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: From where have you come? He said: From my family and children and clan. He said: Then where do you intend? He said: I intend the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Then you have found him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me what faith is. He said: You bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and you establish the prayer, and you pay the alms, and you fast Ramadan, and you perform Hajj to the House. He said: I affirm. He said: Then his camel's foreleg entered the burrow network of rats, so his camel fell and the man fell and landed on his crown and died. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bring me the man. He said: So Ammar ibn Yasir and Hudhayfah sprang to him and sat him up, and said: O Messenger of Allah, the man is dead. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned away from them. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: Did you not see my turning away from the two men? For I saw two angels feeding into his mouth of the fruits of Paradise, so I knew that he died hungry. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This, by Allah, is among those of whom Allah, mighty and majestic is He, said: Those who believe and do not mix their belief with wrongdoing, for them there is security, and they are guided. He said: Then he said: Take your brother. He said: So we carried him to the water and washed him and embalmed him and shrouded him and carried him to the grave. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came until he sat at the edge of the grave. He said: And he said: Make a lahd and do not make a shaqq, for the lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others."
"19391","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Jafar al-Farra narrated to us from Thabit from Zadham from Jarir ibn Abdillah al-Bajali, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Madinah, and while we were traveling, a figure appeared to us, and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: The foreleg of his young camel fell into one of those holes that rats dig; and he said in it: This is among those who did little and were rewarded much."
"19392","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Zaidah narrated to us: Bayan narrated to us from Qays from Jarir, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never veiled himself from me since I became Muslim, nor saw me but that he smiled."
"19393","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Ismail narrated to me from Qays from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never veiled himself from me since I became Muslim, nor saw me but that he smiled in my face."
"19394","Abu Qatan narrated to us: Yunus narrated to me from al-Mughirah ibn Shibl, he said, and Jarir said: When I drew near Madinah, I made my camel kneel, then I untied my baggage, then I put on my robe, then I entered, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was addressing, so the people stared at me. So I said to my seatmate: O servant of Allah, did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mention me? He said: Yes, he mentioned you just now with the finest mention. And while he was addressing, he said in his address: There shall enter upon you through this door, or through this mountain pass, one of the best of Dhu Yaman, except that upon his face is the touch of an angel. Jarir said: So I praised Allah, mighty and majestic is He, for what He had bestowed upon me. And Abu Qatan said: So I said to him: Did you hear it from him, or did you hear it from al-Mughirah ibn Shibl? He said: Yes."
"19395","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Yunus narrated to us from al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl ibn Awf from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: When I drew near Madinah, I made my camel kneel, then I untied my baggage, then I put on my robe. He said: So I entered while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was addressing, so I greeted the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the people stared at me. So I said to my seatmate: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mention anything of my affair? And he mentioned the like of it."
"19396","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from al-Amash from Abu Wail from Jarir that when he pledged to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he took upon him that he associate nothing with Allah and establish the prayer and pay the alms and give counsel to the Muslim and part from the polytheist."
"19397","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us from Qatadah from Humayd ibn Hilal from Jarir ibn Abdillah al-Bajali that a man from the Ansar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a bundle of gold filling what is between his fingers, and said: This is in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic is He. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, stood, and they gave, and he gave; then Umar, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, stood, and they gave, and he gave; then the Emigrants stood and gave. He said: So the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, brightened until I saw the brightness in his cheeks. Then he said: Whoever institutes a righteous practice in Islam and it is acted upon after him, he shall have the like of their rewards, without anything being diminished from their rewards; and whoever institutes in Islam an evil practice and it is acted upon after him, upon him shall be the like of their burdens, without anything being diminished from their burdens."
"19398","Yahya ibn Zakariyya, and he is Ibn Abi Zaidah, narrated to us: Abu Hayyan al-Taymi narrated to us from al-Dahhak, the maternal uncle of al-Mundhir, from Mundhir ibn Jarir from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: None harbors the stray except one astray."
"19399","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us from Qays from Jarir ibn Abdillah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him to Dhu al-Khalasah, so he demolished it and burned it with fire; then he sent a man from Ahmas called Bushayr to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to bear him glad tidings."
"19400","Abu Ahmad, and he is al-Zubayri, narrated to us: Sharik, and he is Ibn Abdillah, narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Amir from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so seek forgiveness for him."
"19401","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud informed us, from Amir, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The zakat collector should depart while he is satisfied with you."
"19402","Yazid narrated to us, Ismail informed us, from Qays, he said: Jarir ibn Abdillah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Will you not relieve me of Dhu al-Khalasah, and it was a house in Khatham called Kabat al-Yamaniyah, so I set out to it with seventy and one hundred horsemen of Ahmas, he said: Then he came to it and burned it with fire, and Jarir sent a bearer of glad tidings to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: By Him Who sent you with the truth, I did not come to you until I left it as if it were a mangy camel, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, blessed the horses of Ahmas and its men five times."
"19403","Yazid narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: Jarir said to me: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah Almighty will not show mercy to him."
"19404","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail, he said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrating from Jarir, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the night of the full moon, and he said: You will see your Lord Almighty as you see the moon, you will not suffer crowding in seeing Him, so if you are able not to be overcome regarding these two prayers, before sunrise and before sunset, then recite this verse: So glorify with praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset. Shubah said: I do not know whether he said: If you are able, or he did not say it."
"19405","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail, he said: I heard Qays narrating from Jarir, he said: I pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon establishing prayer and giving zakah and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"19406","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are no people who practice sins, and among them is a man mightier than them and more able to prevent, and they do not change it, except Allah Almighty encompasses them with punishment, or he said: Punishment befalls them."
"19407","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: I heard Jarir saying, when al-Mughirah died and he employed his relative, addressing: Then Jarir stood and said: I advise you to fear Allah alone, with no partner for Him, and to hear and obey until an amir comes to you, seek forgiveness for al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, may Allah Almighty forgive him, for he loved well-being. As for after: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to pledge him with this hand of mine upon Islam, and he stipulated upon me sincere advice, so by the Lord of this mosque, I am surely sincere to you."
"19408","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, he said: Jarir ibn Abdillah was in an expedition in Arminiyah, he said: Hunger or famine befell them, he said: So Jarir wrote to Muawiyah: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah Almighty will not show mercy to him, he said: So he sent to him and he came to him, and he said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Yes, he said: So he sent them back with provision and supplied them. Abu Ishaq said: And my father was in that army, and he brought a velvet cloak from what Muawiyah supplied."
"19409","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jarir, he said: I pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon hearing and obeying, and he said: So he prompted me, and he said: In what you are able, and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"19410","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zarah ibn Amr, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, twisting the forelock of a horse with his two fingers, saying: Horses have good tied to their forelocks, reward and spoils, until the Day of Resurrection."
"19411","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zarah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the sudden glance, and he commanded me and said: Turn away your sight."
"19412","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Shabi, from Jarir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The zakat collector should depart from you while satisfied."
"19413","Sufyan narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated to us, he said: I heard Jarir saying: I pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon sincere advice to every Muslim. Misar said, from Ziyad: For I am surely sincere to you."
"19414","Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abu Wail, from Jarir, that some Bedouin people came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wearing striped woolen cloaks with slits, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, urged people to charity, and they were slow until that was seen in his face, then a man of the Ansar came with a piece of uncoined gold and threw it down, then people followed one another until that was recognized in his face, then he said: Whoever establishes a good practice and it is acted upon after him, he has its reward and like the reward of whoever acts upon it, without anything being diminished from their rewards, and whoever establishes an evil practice and it is acted upon after him, upon him is its burden and the burden of whoever acts upon it, and that does not diminish anything from their burdens."
"19415","Sufyan narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, he said: I saw Jarir ibn Abdillah performing ablution from a vessel for purification and wiping over his leather socks, and they said: Do you wipe over your leather socks, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said once: Wiping over his leather socks, and this hadith used to please the companions of Abdillah, saying: His Islam was only after the revelation of al-Maidah."
"19416","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim, meaning Ibn Subayh, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal al-Absi, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and urged us to charity, and people were slow until anger was seen in his face, and he said once: Until it became clear, then a man of the Ansar came with a purse and gave it to him, then people followed and gave until joy was seen in his face, then he said: Whoever establishes a good practice, he has its reward and like the reward of whoever acts upon it, without anything being diminished from their rewards, and whoever establishes an evil practice, upon him is its burden and like the burden of whoever acts upon it, without anything being diminished from their burdens, he said once, meaning Abu Muawiyah: Without decreasing."
"19417","Abu Muawiyah, and he is al-Darir, narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah Almighty will not show mercy to him."
"19418","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ismail, he said: Qays narrated to me, he said: Jarir ibn Abdillah said to me: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Will you not relieve me of Dhu al-Khalasah, and it was a house in Khatham called Kabat al-Yamaniyah, he said: So I set out with fifty and one hundred horsemen of Ahmas, and they were horsemen, and I informed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that I am not firm upon horses, so he struck my chest until I saw the trace of his fingers on my chest, and said: O Allah, make him firm and make him guiding, guided, so he set out to it and broke it and burned it, then he sent to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, giving him glad tidings, and the messenger of Jarir said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: By Him Who sent you with the truth, I did not come to you until I left it as if it were a mangy camel, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, blessed the horses of Ahmas and its men five times."
"19419","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Qays narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abdillah said to me: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon, and said: You will surely see your Lord Almighty as you see this, you will not suffer crowding, or you will not suffer harm, Ismail doubted, in seeing Him, so if you are able not to be overcome regarding a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so, then he said: So glorify with praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset."
"19420","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail, Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal al-Absi narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abdillah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No servant establishes a righteous practice that those after him act upon, except he has like the reward of whoever acts upon it, nothing being diminished from their rewards, and no servant establishes an evil practice that those after him act upon, except upon him is its burden and the burden of whoever acts upon it, nothing being diminished from their burdens. He said: And some Bedouin people came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, some of your zakat collectors come to us wronging us, he said: Satisfy your zakat collectors even if wronged, he said: Satisfy your zakat collectors. Jarir said: No zakat collector departed from me since I heard it from the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except while he was satisfied with me. He said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."
"19421","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan, he said: al-Dahhak, uncle of al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, narrated to me, from Mundhir ibn Jarir, from Jarir, he said: I was with my father Jarir at al-Bawarij in al-Sawad, and I was herding cattle, and he saw a cow he did not recognize, and said: What is this cow, he said: A cow that joined the cattle, so he ordered it to be driven away until it disappeared, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No one shelters a stray animal except one who is astray."
"19422","Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from Jarir, he said: He did not veil himself from me since I embraced Islam, nor did he see me except he smiled in my face."
"19423","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Mughirah ibn Shibl, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a slave flees, the covenant is free from him."
"19424","Abdillah said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Mukharrimi narrated to me, al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, a son of Jarir ibn Abdillah narrated to me, he said: The sandal of Jarir ibn Abdillah was a cubit in length."
"19425","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Yaqzan Uthman ibn Umayr al-Bajali, from Zadhan, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The niche grave is for us, and the trench grave is for the People of the Book."
"19426","Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, and Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, from Tariq al-Tamimi, from Jarir, Ibn Jafar said: A man narrated to me, from Tariq al-Tamimi, from Jarir, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by women and greeted them."
"19427","Waki narrated to us, from Sharik, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another, and the freed captives of Quraysh and the freed slaves of Thaqif are allies of one another until the Day of Resurrection."
"19428","Sharik said: Al-Amash narrated to us, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal, from Jarir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"19429","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdillah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are no people among whom is one who practices sins, they mightier than him and more able to prevent, and they do not change it, except Allah Almighty strikes them with punishment from him."
"19430","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mudrik, he said: I heard Abu Zarah ibn Amr ibn Jarir narrating from Jarir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in the Farewell Pilgrimage to Jarir: Make people listen quietly, and he said: He said: Do not return after me disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"19431","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Musa ibn Abdillah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal al-Absi, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The freed captives of Quraysh and the freed slaves of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter, and the Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."
"19432","Abu Abd al-Rahman Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Jarir, he said: I said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Stipulate upon me, he said: Worship Allah, associate nothing with Him, perform the prescribed prayer, give the obligatory zakah, advise the Muslim, and disavow the disbeliever."
"19433","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Islam is built upon five: testimony that there is no god but Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan."
"19434","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdillah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al-Jazari, from Mujahid, from Jarir ibn Abdillah al-Bajali, he said: I embraced Islam after al-Maidah was revealed, and I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping after I embraced Islam."
"19435","Musa ibn Dawud and Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so seek forgiveness for him."
"19436","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Jarir, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Jarir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to enter the privy in his leather socks, then come out and perform ablution and wipe over them."
"19437","Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdillah said: And I heard it myself from Ibn Abi Shaybah, he said: Abdillah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to Yemen, and I met there two men, Dhu Kala and Dhu Amr, he said: And I informed them something of the news of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Then we came forward, and a caravan from the direction of Madinah appeared before us, he said: So we asked them what is the news, he said: So they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has died, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, has succeeded, and people are righteous, he said: Then he said to me: Inform your companion, he said: So they returned, then I met Dhu Amr, and he said to me: O Jarir, you will remain in good as long as, when an amir dies, you then appoint another in authority, but if it is by the sword, you anger with the anger of kings and are pleased with the pleasure of kings."
"19438","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Dawud, meaning Ibn Yazid al-Awdi, narrated to us, from Amir, from Jarir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When a slave flees and joins the enemy and dies, he is a disbeliever."
"19439","Makki narrated to us, Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi narrated to us, from Amir, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Islam is built upon five: testimony that there is no god but Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan."
"19440","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Shibl, he said: Jarir said: When I drew near Madinah, I made my mount kneel, then untied my baggage, then wore my suit, then entered the mosque, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was preaching, and people stared at me, he said: So I said to my companion: O servant of Allah, did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mention anything of my matter, he said: Yes, he mentioned you with the best mention, while he was preaching something occurred to him in his sermon, and he said: There will enter upon you from this pass among the best of Dhu Yaman, indeed upon his face is the touch of an angel. Jarir said: So I praised Allah Almighty."
"19441","Sufyan narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jarir, he said: I pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon establishing prayer and giving zakah and hearing and obeying and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"19442","Ismail narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zarah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, he said: Jarir said: I pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon hearing and obeying, and upon advising every Muslim, he said: And Jarir, when he bought something and it pleased him more than its price, said to its owner: Know, by Allah, what we took is dearer to us than what we gave you, as if intending thereby fulfillment."
"19443","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating from Ubaydillah ibn Jarir, from his father, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are no people among whom sins are practiced, they mightier and more numerous than those who practice it, and they do not change it, except Allah encompasses them with punishment."
"19444","Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Mujalid ibn Said informed us, from al-Shabi, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the zakat collector comes to you, he should not leave you except with satisfaction."
"19445","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated to us, from Jarir, he said: A Jewish scholar in Yemen said to me: If your companion is a prophet, then he has died today. Jarir said: So he died on Monday, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"19446","Abu Said narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Jarir, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, stipulate upon me, for you know better the stipulation, he said: I pledge you to worship Allah, associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, advise the Muslim, and disavow the polytheist."
"19447","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, that Jarir ibn Abdillah urinated and performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, and it was said to him, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, doing it. Ibrahim said: What pleased them most is that the Islam of Jarir was after al-Maidah."
"19448","He narrated to us - [source text truncated at this word, remainder garbled or missing]."
"19449","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Jarir, that he urinated, he said: Then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks and prayed, and he was asked about that, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do like this, he said: And this hadith used to please them, because Jarir was among the last to embrace Islam."
"19450","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Shubah, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, that Jarir urinated standing, then performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks and prayed, so I asked him about that, and he mentioned from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he did like that."
"19451","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Nuhaylah, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to pledge him, and I said: Give your hand and stipulate upon me, and you know better the stipulation, and he said: I pledge you to not associate anything with Allah, and to establish prayer, and to give zakah, and to advise the Muslim, and to separate from the polytheist."
"19452","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir, from Jarir, he said: When he flees to the land of polytheism, meaning the slave, he has made himself lawful, and Sharik perhaps raised it to the Prophet."
"19453","Abu Ahmad, and he is al-Zubayri, narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir, from Jarir, and he did not raise it, he said: When a slave flees to the land of the enemy, his blood has become lawful."
"19454","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from his father, from Jarir, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah Almighty will not show mercy to him."
"19455","Abdillah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdillah said: And I heard it myself from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, Hafs narrated to us, from Dawud, from Amir al-Shabi, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any slave who flees has become free from the covenant."
"19456","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Shabi, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any slave who flees from his masters has disbelieved."
"19457","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn Qarm, narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: I heard Jarir saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, and whoever does not forgive will not be forgiven."
"19458","Yahya, and he is Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from Jarir, he said: I pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon establishing prayer and giving zakah and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"19459","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Amir, from Jarir, and Abdah said: Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Jarir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When the zakat collector comes to you, he should not leave you except while satisfied."
"19460","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Qays narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah Almighty will not show mercy to him."
"19461","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Qays narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: I pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon establishing prayer and giving zakah and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"19462","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, from Jarir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Will you not relieve me of Dhu al-Khalasah, a house of Khatham worshipped in ignorance, called Kabat al-Yamaniyah, he said: So we went out to it with fifty and one hundred riders, he said: So we destroyed it or burned it until we left it like a mangy camel, he said: Then Jarir sent to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, giving him glad tidings of that, he said: So when he came to him, he said: By Him Who sent you with the truth, O Messenger of Allah, I did not come to you until we left it like a mangy camel, he said: So he blessed Ahmas and its horses and its men five times, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man not firm upon horses, so he placed his hand upon my face until I felt its coolness, and said: O Allah, make him guiding, guided."
"19463","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ismail said, Qays said, Jarir said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not veil himself from me since I embraced Islam, nor did he see me ever except he smiled."
"19464","Waki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon, and said: You will surely be presented to your Lord Almighty and see Him as you see this moon, you will not suffer crowding, so if you are able not to be overcome regarding a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so, then he recited: So glorify with praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset."
"19465","Waki narrated to us, and Abu Muawiyah, and he is al-Darir, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, from Tamim ibn Salamah al-Sulami, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hilal al-Absi, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."
"19466","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubaydillah ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are no people among whom sins are practiced, they mightier than them and more able to prevent, and they do not change, except Allah Almighty encompasses them with His punishment."
"19467","Hajjaj narrated it to us, Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, then he mentioned its meaning."
"19468","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubaydillah ibn Jarir, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned its meaning."
"19469","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Mundhir, Abdillah said: I think it is from Jarir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: No people practiced, then he mentioned it."
"19470","Aswad narrated it to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubaydillah ibn Jarir, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned it."
"19471","Abd al-Rahman, and he is Ibn Mahdi, narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: I heard Jarir ibn Abdillah upon the pulpit saying: I pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he stipulated upon me sincere advice to every Muslim, for I am surely sincere to you."
"19472","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mudrik, from Abu Zarah, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Make people listen quietly: Do not return after me disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"19473","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, he said: It reached us that Jarir said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Make people listen quietly, then he said at that: I will surely know, after what I see, you returning after me disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"19474","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Umayrah, and he was the guide of al-Asha in ignorance, narrating from Jarir, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I pledge you upon Islam, he said: So he withheld his hand and said: And sincere advice to every Muslim."
"19475","Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah Almighty will not show mercy to him."
"19476","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubaydillah ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah Almighty will not show mercy to him."
